{"id":"F1087","verdict":"accept","strength":"weak","label":"1B","direction":"against","note":"Not re-verified (PCC API returned 429). The consistent ~15% gap between opening bid and award is mostly a Taiwanese procurement artifact: a single bidder opens at budget and is negotiated down to the buyer's secret floor (底價), which is typically about 85% of budget. Taiwan CDC's −15.4% (F983) shows the same pattern. So the gap reflects the buyer's floor-setting habit, not Illumina's discount policy. It still shows no acceleration through 2025, and the 2025 NTU concession (−10%) was smaller."},
{"id":"F1088","verdict":"accept","strength":"weak","label":"2B","direction":"supports","note":"Not re-verified (429). The figures are contract ceilings, and the 2025 lot's scope changed to sample-prep reagents only, so this is not a like-for-like spend decline. Relabeled from 2A to 2B. The more likely explanation is substitution: the same NTU College of Medicine bought an AVITI24 and signed a NT$13.3M AVITI reagent contract from Dec 2025 (F885, D084). See the derived item."},
